            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0806" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4222: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-08T21:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 8,
                                1922—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 12—11:43 a.m.]<anchor
                            n="14" xml:id="d422-f1"/></dateline></opener>
                <p>40. My 38, February 4, 3 p.m. President has sent reply to Chang Tso-lin saying
                    that Cabinet was formed because Chang and Tsao Kun agreed to it and not because
                    of any previously formed purpose <pb facs="0807" n="687" xml:id="pg687"/> of the
                    President himself and that Shantung matter having been twice explained by Liang
                    Cabinet no further explanation is necessary and Chang is requested to determine
                    in direct consultation with Tsao what measures must now be taken.</p>
                <p>Chang holding conference Mukden and Tsao and Wu Pei-fu at Paotingfu in regard to
                    Cabinet. Crisis continuing difficult yet neither wants to fight partly for
                    military reasons and partly because Liang does not make a popular issue for
                    Chang nor the Chihli party for Wu.</p>
                <p>At noon today Liang stated privately that while preferring to resign he would not
                    take any action before the 13th and that plans for ousting President had been
                    perfected.</p>
                <p>Unless Government grapples with fundamental issues of reunion of provinces and
                    financial rehabilitation Cabinet changes matter little. More changes more the
                    same thing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
